reims-vgpu: the frame mailbox hand-off copy uses streaming stores.

The present drain copies the BGRA8 retain (12.6 MB) into the mailbox
writer's hand-off buffer in up to four bands; the writer thread, not the
drain, reads it next. Each band now copies with non-temporal stores and
fences before its thread ends, so the hand-off's old lines are not read
first and its new ones not kept in the drain's cache. The bytes are the
same.

A recorded live run on the development host (1.2.1 engine) spends 1.06 ms an
offer, against 0.3-0.5 ms offline with both buffers in the cache: on a live
phone they are mostly not. Offline (banded_copy_timing, medians of 31, two
runs on a shared host): with 96 MB of other writes before each copy, ordinary
bands 1.7-1.8 ms against streamed 1.2-1.4 ms; with both buffers in the cache,
0.3-0.6 ms against 0.6-0.7 ms. Not measured on a live phone.

